  "beats": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "sectionIndex": 0,
      "section": "Nineteen percent",
      "text": "19%. That is how many patients cleared chronic Hepatitis B after a six-month course of GSK's new drug Hibsago, approved by the FDA on October 20th.",
      "cue": null,
      "startMs": 200,
      "endMs": 12030
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "sectionIndex": 1,
      "section": "For life",
      "text": "Current treatments keep the virus suppressed for life. Fewer than one in a hundred clear it in a year.",
      "cue": null,
      "startMs": 12030,
      "endMs": 17950
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "sectionIndex": 2,
      "section": "Two firsts",
      "text": "Hibsago is the first antisense oligonucleotide ever approved in this disease, and the first drug ever to target a functional cure in a six-month course.",
      "cue": null,
      "startMs": 17950,
      "endMs": 28240
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "sectionIndex": 3,
      "section": "A narrow label",
      "text": "The label is narrow. Adults without cirrhosis, already on antivirals for at least six months, with low surface antigen levels.",
      "cue": null,
      "startMs": 28240,
      "endMs": 36450
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "sectionIndex": 4,
      "section": "A different frame",
      "text": "But 240 million people live with chronic Hep B worldwide. For an indication that was lifelong, that is a different frame.",
      "cue": null,
      "startMs": 36450,
      "endMs": 45234
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "sectionIndex": 4,
      "section": "A different frame",
      "text": "The read on winners, losers, and the payer calendar is in this week's Catalyst Brief. Subscribe free, signal over noise.",
      "cue": null,
      "startMs": 45234,
      "endMs": 53080
    }
  ],
